  "id": "redintegration",
  "term": "redintegration",
  "definition": "Redintegration is the rebuilding of a memory trace in working memory by drawing on information stored in long-term memory. In verbal working memory, it refers to using existing knowledge, such as vocabulary, to help reconstruct what was being held in mind.",
